{
  "_comment": [
    "Numeric skill-effect families for the advanced search (min/max range filters).",
    "Each matcher's regex is applied with flags 'gi' to the skill description column",
    "for its skill_type; value_group is the capture group holding the number.",
    "A monster matches a family range if ANY occurrence of ANY of its matchers",
    "yields a value inside [min, max]. min_observed/max_observed/cards_observed are",
    "documentation only (measured against the dadguide snapshot) and drive UI hints.",
    "Regexes deliberately use [^.;]*? rather than [^.]*? so a matcher cannot jump",
    "across clause boundaries and capture a number belonging to a different effect.",
    "tags: effect chips (pattern tag keys per skill type) each family tunes; a selected chip shows",
    "the family inputs and its range is AND'ed into that chip's clause. supports_turns: the effect",
    "has a 'For N turns,' duration (by-turn filter). supports_value false + value_group 0: presence-only",
    "matcher, the family filters by turns only."
  ],
